+# Publication acceptance notification — 2026-10-18
+
+PUB04 notifies the creator when a track is accepted and published after the pending dialog has closed. PUB05 preserves unread acceptance and dismissal across restarts and account changes. PUB06 provides a direct View track action without interrupting racing. G01/R01/Q01 retain the canonical race, existing publication delivery and native verification.
+
+A green **Track published** banner now names the accepted track and offers **View track** plus a 52-unit dismiss control. It persists across menu changes until the player opens or dismisses it. Active racing, race loading and open dialogs defer its display. The player's current menu and keyboard focus remain in place when it arrives. The existing pending dialog still follows its exact request; closing that dialog after it has shown publication acknowledges the same receipt, avoiding a duplicate banner. Closing it before acceptance leaves notification delivery pending.
+
+Acceptance is recorded when the existing status response supplies a published receipt, before waiting for the local download. The lifecycle emits its normal change signal at that point. The saved workflow retains the track name and an optional notification marker. Per-version acknowledgement files live inside the existing library/server/account workflow directory, separate from locked completed jobs. Restarting recovers unread receipts; repeated status events, failed downloads and controller restarts do not restore dismissed notifications. Earlier unfinished accepted jobs are enrolled; historical completed jobs are not all announced. An acknowledgement storage failure keeps the notification unread and exposes the storage error.
+
+The banner reads cached notification entries and adds no backend requests, status polling, uploads or external notification service. View track retains the confirmed metadata through the original publication cache path and opens the exact acknowledged immutable version in Free Race. It does not require the earlier local download to have succeeded. Existing immediate-success navigation remains. Mouse/touch ownership prevents the banner's actions or drags from activating the underlying menu.
+
+Runtime changes: `game/core/app.gd`, `game/backend/track_lifecycle.gd`, and new `game/ui/publication_notification.gd` with its generated UID. `game/tests/test_publication_notifications.gd` and its UID exercise real disposable workflow journals, a held local download, the actual Publish callback, menu/race deferral, account fencing, failed dismissal saves, controller restart, multiple receipts, mouse/touch/drag actions, exact View track receipt identity, old unfinished receipts and pending-dialog deduplication. The existing discovery fixture now returns accepted sharing consent; its assertions are unchanged.
+
+Pinned Godot 4.7.2 checks pass: notification **54 headless / 54 Compatibility / 54 desktop Mobile**, previous publication dialog **72**, existing local publication **31** (real creator lap 2605 ticks/436 samples), discovery **22**, final App **140**, parser **867 scripts**, and editor import. Both renderer runs capture 960×540, 1280×720 and 1600×720 views, plus a supplemental resized window and the notification after a simulated race-owned screen. [Native banner](evidence/publication-notification-2026-10-18/compatibility/published-1280x720.png) and [menu return](evidence/publication-notification-2026-10-18/compatibility/published-after-race.png) are local fixture views, not evidence of any live account publication or device race.
+
+Initial fixture attempts are retained. A helper named `seed` resolved to GDScript's built-in void function and was renamed. A strict receipt comparison first mixed integer fixture values with JSON-decoded floating numbers; the mock receipt now takes the same JSON round trip as real API/journal data, retaining the full equality assertion. The older discovery mock omitted the sharing-consent response required by the current app, causing its initial success assertion to fail; adding that response passes all 22 original assertions. Concurrent publishing-slot, creator and Rivalry work is preserved and excluded from this task's patch; the final current App/local-publication/parser checks include those sources. No failing gameplay assertion was weakened.
+
+[Actual commands, outcomes and hashes](evidence/publication-notification-2026-10-18/report.json) and the [task-only patch](evidence/publication-notification-2026-10-18/task-only.patch) are retained with snapshots, logs and native captures. Owner appearance and live service/device acceptance remain. This is an in-game notification; no closed-app OS push service is added. No phone attachment check or physical-device test, APK/export/install, live publication, backend mutation or deployment was performed.
